2. DATASET & LABELS — CC BY 4.0 (Attribution 4.0 International)
================================================================================

Applies to: benchmark/citations-in-the-wild.v0.json, benchmark/README.md, work/records/*.json,
and any other file that carries record selection, per-citation segmentation, verdict labels, or
the benchmark's structured schema ("the Dataset").

The underlying court decisions quoted and cited by the Dataset are public record and are not
themselves subject to this licence — see benchmark/README.md §3. What is licensed here is the
Dataset's original contribution on top of that public record: which citations were selected, how
each was segmented into a record, the verdict labels (EXISTS_FAIL / SAYS_FAIL / PASS) and finding
taxonomy assigned to each, and the schema itself.

The Dataset is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0). Human-readable summary (not a substitute for the licence):

  You are free to:
    Share   — copy and redistribute the Dataset in any medium or format
    Adapt   — remix, transform, and build upon the Dataset for any purpose, even commercially

  Under the following terms:
    Attribution — You must give appropriate credit to "Citations in the Wild", provide a link
    to this repository, and indicate if changes were made. You may do so in any reasonable
    manner, but not in any way that suggests the licensor endorses you or your use.

    No additional restrictions — You may not apply legal terms or technological measures that
    legally restrict others from doing anything the licence permits.

  No warranties are given. Court findings are transcribed in good faith from published opinions;
  see benchmark/README.md §5 for known limits.

Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

